\details{
Four conditions that are often merged are kept apart:
\itemize{
\item reference \code{"unknown"}: correctness cannot be assessed;
\item response \code{"no_input"}: the reference may be known, but the monitor had no input, so a prediction was impossible;
\item response \code{"abstain"}: input was available and the detector declined;
\item response \code{"negative"}: an actual "no event" answer that can be right or wrong.
